    schema:description "Identified 2026-07-14, then corrected same day: preferences.ttl had gates for external shared-vocabulary discovery (prefix.cc) and real-world entity IRI denotation, but none for reusing THIS AGENT'S OWN previously-minted, DAV-published, resolver-dereferenceable document-local DefinedTerms/classes/properties (e.g. avc:abac, karp:CriticalPerspective). Initial framing wrongly conditioned reuse on the new document being a topically-related companion/sequel; the user clarified that resolver-IRI dereferenceability makes any minted term reusable in ANY future task regardless of topic — the point is preventing custom term bloat across the full output corpus, not just within a series."@en ;
