    schema:description "User audit of the 'Why Open Source Matters for AI' KG (oreillyradar.substack.com guest post by Tim O'Reilly) found glossary/topic DefinedTerms and people minted as document-local hash IRIs, violating preferences.ttl#step-crossDocumentLocalTermReuse (pos 127) and howto/canonical-entity-iri-denotation.ttl. Remediation: verified canonical targets (DBpedia /data JSON self-node, Wikidata EntityData with UA, Wikipedia status, web search) then rewrote the TTL (478 triples) with canonical IRIs as sole subjects — 10 glossary terms + 6 topic dupes consolidated (Open Source/MCP/Agentic AI/Composability/LAMP -> DBpedia; AI Sovereignty -> wikidata:Q140561783 Sovereign AI; Open Weights/Harness/Distribution Convergence/Architecture of Participation stay document-local), 9 people moved to platform #this IRIs (Tim linkedin.com/in/timo3#this user-provided, X/Substack/GitHub via owl:sameAs; Addy x.com/addyosmani#this; Mario github.com/badlogic#this; Bob/Bill DBpedia; Isobel ssrc profile; Ilan personal site), organizations/software canonicalized too, Rule-19 enrichment, owl:sameAs entity-IRI-only + schema:sameAs for document URLs. GATE: validate-kg-compliance.sh 15/15 PASS; HTML 63 resolver links updated (28 canonicalized, 0 stale, 0 double-encoded), JSON-LD author @id + canonical skill @ids added, tag balance clean, node --check OK. Verified-with-caveats: Tim LinkedIn URL HTTP 999 bot-block (user supplied https://www.linkedin.com/in/timo3 on 2026-08-11); Architecture of Participation Wikipedia 404 (no article); Wikidata batch wbgetentities flaky 403/429 (retry per-ID); URIBurner person census SPARQL timed out twice. Follow-up: hero OBO ('Generated on behalf of Kingsley Idehen') attribution added per user clarification that OBO = on behalf of, hero section only; HTML now 64 resolver links, all gates re-pass."@en .

