    schema:description "Generated the x402-buyer skill from a user-supplied zip (x402_test.zip) containing a single x402 v2 buyer-side Python client, x402_get.py. Built it out to this repo's skill conventions (acp-client / mpp-stripe-client as structural models): SKILL.md with YAML frontmatter and trigger phrases, scripts/x402_get.py (verbatim), references/{setup,protocol,troubleshooting}.md, examples/{probe-challenge,local-dav}.sh. Two judgment additions beyond the source: a no-cost challenge-probe + base64-decode step (a 402 in this repo's world may be x402 OR Stripe/MPP, so the protocol must be identified before committing to a client), and a Payment Gate checklist (an x402 run signs an irreversible on-chain EIP-3009 authorization). Documented the two same-version-number x402 SDK sources whose only difference is set_spend_controls, i.e. whether --max-amount is actually enforced. All URLs verbatim from the source script; no fabricated URLs. x402-buyer.zip repackaged per the standing ZIP rule. Flagged to the user that the upstream script's docstring carried a throwaway Base Sepolia buyer private key; the user then asked for it to be moved to the Keychain and prompted for when required, which was done (service x402-buyer-evm-key, four-source resolver, key literal stripped and swept from both the skill dir and the ZIP, skill bumped to 1.1.0) and generalised into preferences.ttl Step 235 + howto/secret-resolution-in-generated-skills.ttl. Session continued (model switched mid-session to Claude Sonnet 5, Step 222): corrected cross-platform key-access docs (keyring required not optional off macOS, headless-Linux caveat, honest macOS-only-tested scope, 1.1.0 -> 1.1.1); live-probed a real x402-protected OPL Shop resource on ods-qa.openlinksw.com, first plain then with the user's WebID-TLS cert, discovering the WebID-TLS handshake lives on port 5443 not 443; user asked both x402-buyer and acp-client be tweaked to default to 5443 automatically, done as x402-buyer's first-ever client-certificate support (rewrite_for_webid_tls, resolve_cert_passphrase under a separate credential-store service, extract_pem_from_p12 as the sanctioned PEM-extraction exception, 1.1.1 -> 1.2.0) and acp-client's Auth-Protocol-Selection RULE promotion (1.6.0 -> 1.7.0); also found and fixed a latent macOS-awk-IGNORECASE portability bug in the challenge-decode pipeline discovered while live-testing the fix. Full pipeline verified end-to-end against the real resource with the principal's real cert. Generalised into preferences.ttl Steps 236-237 + howto/webid-tls-port-5443-default.ttl."@en .

